# Project Dossier and Harness Adoption

> This checklist records work; checking a box does not create authority or
> prove substantive readiness.

- [ ] Applicable root-to-leaf instructions were read.
- [ ] Project scope, exclusions, outcomes, and stakeholders were adopted.
- [ ] Authority sources and external-action gates were recorded.
- [ ] Canonical source owners and conflict rules were adopted.
- [ ] Artifact types, physical representations, source direction, owners, and
      review state were reconciled in the authoritative artifact registry.
- [ ] Every conditional and optional trigger was assessed as `applicable` or
      `not_applicable` with `assessed_on`, `assessed_by`, and a rationale; none
      remains silently assumed. Applicable High-Assurance controls have owners,
      active reviewed representations, and current evidence references.
- [ ] Repository, operational, and external current state was directly
      inspected and dated.
- [ ] Requirements, findings, plan items, RAIDQ entries, and evidence use
      stable references.
- [ ] Every project test, lint, build, and closure hook was configured with a
      safe argv contract or marked `not_applicable` with owner and rationale.
- [ ] Configured hooks ran only through the explicit evidence writer; current
      fingerprint-bound results, skips, limitations, dirty scope, and declared
      effects were recorded.
- [ ] Needed domain extensions were registered, validated, and assigned.
- [ ] Read-only validation and mutation tests passed in a clean runtime without
      executing project hooks or creating evidence.
- [ ] Registry-derived catalog, path authority, manifest, and integrity were
      refreshed and rechecked; High-Assurance checksums were included when
      applicable.
- [ ] A real task was completed or handed off using the lifecycle.
- [ ] Unknowns, skipped checks, limitations, and external effects were
      disclosed.
